ource-facing `exists_pulled_apart_consistency`, which constructs a witness and uses other specialized estimates, from this auxiliary. The new main-side `exists_extractionWitness` in `Extraction/SourceUnitary.lean` separately composes a global constructor and a conditional extraction theorem; its chapter-16 node and extraction-transfer register row do not claim to use or discharge `nonencodingMarginalMass_le`. The later isometry range-projection transfer remains open. The source's unrestricted decoder substitution at `references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:1483-1492` is still documented as false, not asserted by the new auxiliary. The inherited `sorry` in `Consistency.lean:650` is unrelated to this theorem.\n\nPrior F1 remains resolved: the audit begins with `title`, `date`, `purpose`, `issue`, and `pr` YAML fields, and its body after the ten-line header has the same SHA-256 `d3cf172f5bb5c12bf1bfab3b8b3dedcf7f5fb47cb81b4b9081a2eac77b0c4eb4` as at `4bd78e34`. It retains PR 543's failed build-lock/blueprint-sync attempt and absent review as historical failures rather than claiming their success.\n\nExact-head GitHub CI read through the primary `gh_common.py` reports all nine `local-ci/*` contexts successful, including build, blueprint render/sync, proof-debt and proof-evasion (summary: 308 seconds). `git diff --check` passed. No new Lean elaboration, full build, CI or whole-proof review was run for this bounded recheck; the earlier proof/axiom evidence and current exact-head CI are used within their stated scope.\n\nVERDICT: APPROVED\n", "state": "COMMENTED", "html_url": "https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-A/pull/580#pullrequestreview-5244004306", "pull_request_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-A/pulls/580", "author_association": "OWNER", "_links": {"html": {"href": "https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-A/pull/580#pullrequestreview-5244004306"}, "pull_request": {"href": "https://api.github.com/repos/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE